Subject: GE Plus: a switch for the GoldenEye XBLA release, on by default

The user wants the GoldenEye XBLA release to have an off switch in the iOS
settings, the way Perfect Dark's own release has (D-019, D-032): off is
GoldenEye's N64 look in GE Plus, without taking the release out of the
added-content folder. Upstream had exactly that key, Mod.XblaGoldenEye
("Enable GoldenEye Characters"), and retired it in be757a939 (2026-09-21)
because it was OFF by default and a player who had put the release in the
right folder still saw none of it. The port followed the retirement (D-072:
no switch). This brings the key back ON by default (D-081), which keeps the
reason upstream retired it answered: adding the release still needs nothing
else.

Off is "the release is not here": gebeanLocate() returns before it scans, so
archivePath and rootPath stay empty, gebeanIsAvailable() and
gebeanGetEnabled() say no (GoldenEye X borrowing is left alone), nothing is
unpacked at startup, the Combat Simulator pool is built from GE Plus's own
converted characters (gebeanPoolRefreshRom()), and every one of the ~26
gebeanGetEnabled() call sites (HD levels, props, guns, skies, menu art, hit
puffs, the HUD) takes the path it takes with no release added - a state the
port already ships and tests. Gating gebeanGetEnabled() alone was the old
switch's shape, but the pool and gun refreshes now ask gebeanIsAvailable(),
so it would leave the release's characters in the pool with nothing to draw.

The value is read ONCE a run, the first time anything asks (after
configInit()): gebeanPoolRefresh() and gebeanUnpackAtStartup() build from the
release at startup, so a release that disappeared mid-run would strand the
pool's rows. A change takes effect the next time the game starts; the
settings page says so, and the shell saves pd.ini as soon as the row moves.

diff --git a/port/include/gebean.h b/port/include/gebean.h
index ce3af719d..b18c84e9b 100644
--- a/port/include/gebean.h
+++ b/port/include/gebean.h
@@ -62,6 +62,13 @@ struct modelnode;
 /** Whether there is GoldenEye content to draw on: the release, or GoldenEye X to borrow from. */
 s32 gebeanGetEnabled(void);
 
+/**
+ * Mod.XblaGoldenEye (overlay 0050): whether the player has the GoldenEye XBLA
+ * release switched on. Read once a run, at the first ask; off is the same as
+ * the release not being there.
+ */
+s32 gebeanSwitchIsOn(void);
+
 /** Whether a copy was found in xbla/, unpacked or not. Never unpacks. */
 s32 gebeanIsAvailable(void);
 
diff --git a/port/src/gebean.c b/port/src/gebean.c
index e93f9d462..afdf50867 100644
--- a/port/src/gebean.c
+++ b/port/src/gebean.c
@@ -2482,6 +2482,46 @@ static char archivePath[FS_MAXPATH + 1]; // what the player dropped, when it is
 static s32 scanned;
 static s32 unpackFailed;
 
+/**
+ * Mod.XblaGoldenEye (overlay 0050, D-081): the player's switch for the
+ * GoldenEye XBLA release, ON by default. Upstream retired the old checkbox of
+ * this name on 2026-09-21 because it was OFF by default and a player who had
+ * added the release saw none of it; the port's settings page wants the switch
+ * back so the release can be turned off for GoldenEye's own N64 look, the way
+ * Perfect Dark's release can.
+ *
+ * Off means the release is not here at all: gebeanLocate() finds nothing, so
+ * gebeanIsAvailable() and gebeanGetEnabled() say no, nothing is unpacked at
+ * startup, the Combat Simulator's pool is GE Plus's own converted characters
+ * (gebeanPoolRefreshRom()) and every HD level, prop, gun and menu picture
+ * falls back exactly as it does with no release added. That is decided once a
+ * run: the pool and the gun rows are built at startup from what the release
+ * gave, and a release that vanished under them mid-run would leave rows with
+ * nothing to draw. So the value is read the first time anything asks, and a
+ * change takes effect the next time the game starts.
+ */
+static s32 switchOn = 1;        // what pd.ini (and the settings page) says
+static s32 switchThisRun = -1;  // what this run went with, at the first look
+
+PD_CONSTRUCTOR static void gebeanSwitchConfigInit(void)
+{
+	configRegisterInt("Mod.XblaGoldenEye", &switchOn, 0, 1);
+}
+
+s32 gebeanSwitchIsOn(void)
+{
+	if (switchThisRun < 0) {
+		switchThisRun = switchOn ? 1 : 0;
+
+		if (!switchThisRun) {
+			sysLogPrintf(LOG_NOTE, "gebean: the GoldenEye XBLA release is switched off (Mod.XblaGoldenEye=0), "
+					"GE Plus keeps GoldenEye's N64 look this run");
+		}
+	}
+
+	return switchThisRun;
+}
+
 /**
  * On when there is GoldenEye content to draw on: the release in added-content/
  * (unpacked or not) or GoldenEye X installed to borrow from. Until 2026-09-21
@@ -2489,6 +2529,7 @@ static s32 unpackFailed;
  * and a player who had put the release in the right folder still saw none of
  * it until they found the box. There is nothing to choose: without the content
  * the switch did nothing, and with it there is no reason to leave it off.
+ * (The port brings the key back ON by default, gebeanSwitchIsOn() above.)
  */
 s32 gebeanGetEnabled(void)
 {
@@ -3566,6 +3607,12 @@ static s32 gebeanLocate(s32 mayUnpack)
 		return 1;
 	}
 
+	// switched off (overlay 0050): as if nothing were in added-content/, so
+	// archivePath stays empty and every caller takes its no-release path
+	if (!gebeanSwitchIsOn()) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!scanned) {
 		scanned = 1;
 
